================================================================================
ANGLE A — mu_min(k) > 0 (HYP-2586): the pure three-distance floor for LRC(14) S3
mac-mini-2026-06-18-S2.  Exact Fractions throughout.
================================================================================

DEFINITION
  mu(E) = meas{ x in [0,1) : {frac(e x): e in E} have circular max-gap > 2/7 }
        = meas{ x : the k points fit in an open arc of length < 5/7 }.
  mu_min(k) = inf over integer sets E (0 in E, |E|=k) of mu(E).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PROVED structural lemmas (exact, verified on samples; proofs in script header)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
L0  REFLECTION   x good <=> 1-x good.  (x->1-x reflects all points about 0;
    max-gap invariant.)  => Good(E) symmetric about 1/2.                  PASS
L1  SCALE INVARIANCE  mu(c*E) = mu(E) for every integer c>=1.
    (x->frac(cx) is c-to-1 measure-preserving; Good(cE) = c disjoint
     1/c-copies of Good(E).)  => mu_min(k)=inf over PRIMITIVE E.          PASS
L2  NEAR-0 INTERVAL  let s=max(E)=spread.  For 0<x<5/(7s) all points
    frac(e x)=e x lie in [0, sx) subset [0,5/7) => arc<5/7 => good.
    Hence (0,5/(7s)) subset Good(E) and  mu(E) >= 5/(7s) > 0
    for EVERY individual integer set E.                                    PASS

  COROLLARY (PROVED):  mu(E) > 0 for every individual E (k>=1).
  The only open content of mu_min(k)>0 is positivity of the INFIMUM.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
k=3  PROVED UNCONDITIONAL:  3 gaps sum to 1 => maxgap >= 1/3 > 2/7.
     mu(E)=1 for ALL |E|=3.  free margin 1/3-2/7 = 1/21.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

EXACT bounded-spread exhaustive minima of mu over PRIMITIVE E (canonical reps):
   k= 3 :  mu_min = 1          = 1.000000   E=[0,1,2]          (spread<=8 exh.)
   k= 4 :  mu_min = 19/21      = 0.904762   E=[0,1,2,3]        (spread<=14 exh.)
   k= 5 :  mu_min = 9/14       = 0.642857   E=[0,1,2,3,4]      (spread<=16 exh.)
   k= 6 :  mu_min = 4/7        = 0.571429   E=[0,1,2,3,4,5]    (spread<=18 exh.)
   k= 7 :  mu_min = 13/35      = 0.371429   E=[0,2,3,4,5,6,8]  (spread<=18 exh.)
   k= 8 :        71/220        = 0.322727   E=[0,2,3,4,5,6,8,11]
   k= 9 :        164/735       = 0.223129   E=[0,2,4,5,6,7,8,9,12]
   k=10 :        214/1365      = 0.156777   E=[0,1,3,4,5,7,9,10,14,15]
   k=11 :        817/5460      = 0.149634   E=[0,1,2,3,4,5,7,9,10,14,15]
   k=12 :        433/3003      = 0.144189   E=[0,1,2,3,4,5,6,8,11,13,14,15]
   k=13 :        5367/35035    = 0.153190   E=[0,1,..,9,12,13,14]
   (k=4,5,6,7 are TRUE minima — exhaustive over all primitive shapes within the
    stated spread bound, which exceeds the observed minimizer spread.
    k=8..13 are exact minima over bounded spread<=14-15, an UPPER BOUND on
    mu_min(k); larger-spread shapes go LOWER — see honest gap below.)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
HONEST GAP (why this is PARTIAL, not a full proof of the infimum for k>=8)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The bounded-spread minima above are NOT the true infimum for large k: random
search over moderate spread (~2k..3k) finds lower values, e.g.
   k=11: mu ~ 0.147 at spread 40,  k=13: mu ~ 0.088 at spread 26.
The minimizer sits at spread O(k) (not at consecutive, not at huge spread):
both extremes RAISE mu (consecutive thins gaps but k<=13 caps it; huge spread
equidistributes => big gaps => high mu).  So the infimum is a MIN over a
BOUNDED-SPREAD family (HYP-2584) — finitely many shapes, each mu>0 exact.

  *** The one missing inequality ***: a RIGOROUS bound  spread(minimizer) <= B(k),
  i.e. "spread > B(k) => mu(E) >= (bounded-spread min)".  L2 gives only
  mu>=5/(7s), which DECREASES with s and so does NOT exclude large spread.
  No clean single-difference uniform bound exists (tested mu>=5/(7 e2): FALSE,
  ratio 0.13 at E=[0,1,5,7,9,10,13,16,18,19,21,25,26]).  This is exactly the
  compact-space uniform-floor crux of THM-527.G.1 / OPEN-Q-108.

NET:  mu_min(k) > 0 is PROVED for k=3 (unconditional) and for every individual
E (L2); the positivity of the INFIMUM for 4<=k<=13 reduces (VERIFIED, not yet
PROVED) to a bounded-spread finite family on which every exact rational is
positive.  LRC(14) S3 remains open on precisely the spread-bound inequality.
================================================================================
